{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Source of the OWNER RIGHTS ACE confirmed (AC1). Throwaway diag branch `w1-diag-opcert-acl` (never merged), `sweep (windows)` run 44581143998, job 135761807560, Python 3.13 on windows-latest, running as runnervmm7ud1\\runneradmin:\n- The runner temp folder `C:\\Users\\RUNNER~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp` carries SYSTEM, Administrators and runneradmin, all (OI)(CI)(F). No OWNER RIGHTS entry, so the second hypothesis (temp folder ACL) is refuted.\n- A fresh `tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"rebar-opcert-\")` dir carries exactly SYSTEM, Administrators and OWNER RIGHTS, all (OI)(CI)(F). The user's own entry is gone, which matches Python 3.13's `os.mkdir(mode=0o700)` on Windows replacing the DACL.\n- The key copy written into it by `keyprov._write_copy` carries exactly SYSTEM:(F), Administrators:(F), OWNER RIGHTS:(F), so it takes its ACL from that dir.\n- `ssh-keygen -y -P \"\" -f <copy>` exits 255 with \"Bad permissions. Try removing permissions for user: \\\\OWNER RIGHTS (S-1-3-4)\".\nAll 28 tests in `openssh-key-acl.args` fail or error with that same OpcertKeyError in the same run.\n\nConclusion: the ACE comes from the DACL that `tempfile.mkdtemp` (Python 3.13 `os.mkdir(mode=0o700)`) writes on the runtime dir. The copy takes that DACL when it is created."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795110665831666556,"uuid":"88499f0f-8e7d-4a26-b759-2dfdb4d223d9"}